  note={.
    Ducournau and Habib exploring the graph properties of inheritance algorithms,
    but not yet having formulated monotonicity.
    They call “multiplicity” (why?) the local precedence order.
    IIUC, their property 1 is linearization, 4 is local precedence order,
    and 2 is their expressing the tie break heuristic as “greediness”,
    i.e. in terms of working with minimal lookahead from the list of available candidates.
    The only thing that’s missing to make it C3 is the monotonicity requirement;
    funny then that they didn’t immediately find that C3 as a solution
    when they invented monotonicity in 1992. Maybe I’m misreading what they mean by “greediness”.
  }
}

